# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its system gitconfig, so without
# this file a Windows checkout writes every text file with CRLF. The index stays
# LF and CI never notices, but Prettier's endOfLine defaults to lf, and
# `npm run format:check` — and so `npm run gates` — fails on hundreds of files
# nobody touched. An attribute outranks autocrlf, so this settles it for every
# clone regardless of how its git was installed.
#
# Renormalizing under these rules changes no committed file: the index was
# already LF throughout when this was added.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The binary types the repository tracks. text=auto would already detect them;
# naming them means no heuristic ever gets to guess about a GLB or a baked map.
*.glb binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
